# .research-sdd/vendor-leak.conf — vendor-code leak guard declaration (kit issue #1271).
# Read by research-sdd/toolbelt/scan-vendor-leak.sh. This target's remote is PUBLIC, so anything
# declared here as vendor code must never be committed. Binaries (*.class *.jar *.dll *.so *.exe)
# are always flagged unless allowed below; the directives that follow are what YOU must declare.
#
#   prefix <java.package.prefix>   vendor package whose declaration in a tracked file is a leak
#   path   <glob>                  repo-relative glob of a tree that holds vendor code (decompiled output)
#   allow  <glob>                  reviewed exception — allow wins over every other rule
#
# Until a prefix or path is declared the scanner reports EMPTY-CONF and applies the binary rule only:
# a clean run then proves nothing about decompiled vendor source. Fill this in (examples, uncomment):
#
# prefix com.vendor.product
# path   decompiled/**
# allow  tools/fixtures/tiny-test.jar
